// Title: Phase 3e - Volume Shadow Copy registry footprint from suspicious parents
// MITRE: T1003.003 (NTDS via VSS), T1006 (Direct Volume Access)
// Data sources: DeviceRegistryEvents
// False positive notes: Backup software (Veeam, Acronis, Windows Backup, SQL VSS writer)
//                       legitimately drives VSS and writes these keys. This query only keeps
//                       events whose initiating process is a hands-on-keyboard / LOLBin parent,
//                       which removes most benign backup noise. Allow-list known backup agents.
// Author: detection pack maintainers
// Date: 2026-06-27
//
// Volt Typhoon and similar actors create a shadow copy to read a locked ntds.dit
// (`vssadmin create shadow`, diskshadow, WMI). VSS leaves diagnostic/settings registry
// writes. Pairing the registry footprint with a LOLBin parent process is the signal.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where RegistryKey has_any (
    @"\Services\VSS\Diag",
    @"\Services\VSS\Settings",
    @"\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Diagnostics\VSS")
| where ActionType in ("RegistryValueSet", "RegistryKeyCreated")
| where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ (
    "cmd.exe", "powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe", "wmic.exe",
    "ntdsutil.exe", "diskshadow.exe", "vssadmin.exe", "esentutl.exe", "wbadmin.exe")
| extend Phase = "CredAccess-VSS-Registry"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, ActionType, RegistryKey, RegistryValueName, RegistryValueData,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName, Phase
| order by Timestamp desc
